.generation-log.json

# Skills the system writes for itself are runtime state, not source. They are
# the product of running Jarvis, they are regenerated on demand, and a fresh
# clone should start with the built-in set only — a clone that already held
# nineteen "learned" skills would misrepresent what the system had done.
#
# The rule is inverted rather than a list of generated names, so a skill
# authored tomorrow is ignored without anyone remembering to add it here.
# Nothing is deleted: ignored skills stay on disk and keep working.
#
# What was generated during evaluation is recorded in
# ClawBenchmark/generation_eval_*.json, which is tracked.
/*/
!/app-launch/
!/app-quit/
!/bluetooth-toggle/
!/display-brightness/
!/file-explore/
!/media-control/
!/screen-capture/
!/system-mute/
!/system-volume/
!/wifi-toggle/
